Use io, list, and string.

Define function letter_start taking digit as a byte returning a byte:
    If digit equals 50, give back 97.
    If digit equals 51, give back 100.
    If digit equals 52, give back 103.
    If digit equals 53, give back 106.
    If digit equals 54, give back 109.
    If digit equals 55, give back 112.
    If digit equals 56, give back 116.
    If digit equals 57, give back 119.
    Give back 97.
Done.

Define function letter_count taking digit as a byte returning an unsigned number:
    If digit equals 55 or digit equals 57:
        Give back 4 as an unsigned number.
    If digit equals 50 or digit equals 51 or digit equals 52 or digit equals 53 or digit equals 54 or digit equals 56:
        Give back 3 as an unsigned number.
    Give back 0 as an unsigned number.
Done.

Define function expand taking digits as a pointer to TcString, depth as an unsigned number, buffer as a pointer to byte, n as an unsigned number:
    If depth equals n:
        Let answer be create text from buffer of length n.
        Say answer.
        str_free(address of answer).
        Give back.
    Let digit be digits.data[depth].
    Let start be letter_start(digit).
    Let choices be letter_count(digit).
    For every k from 0 as an unsigned number to choices - 1:
        Set item depth of buffer to (start as an unsigned number + k) as a byte.
        expand(digits, depth + 1, buffer, n).
Done.

Let digits be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("23"), bytes_len("23")).
Let n be length of address of digits.
Let buffer be block of 8 byte.
expand(address of digits, 0, address of item 0 of buffer, n).
str_free(address of digits).
Return 0.
